This unofficial SwiftUI port adapts the original word/character matching,
numeric reconciliation, animation anchors, grouped replacement, fade timing,
spring sampling, and interrupted container motion. The reference implementation
is commit d79a5aa63226acf97d49c3e34fafb2e85c07b026.

The reference test fixtures were generated from the original library and its
shared test cases. Documentation/BehaviorParity.md maps the original source
files to the Swift implementations and documents native platform differences.

The native SwiftUI rendering, platform integration, and native Spring API are
part of this port, maintained by ikeadrift. Lochie Axon is credited as the
creator of the original Torph library, not as the author or maintainer of these
Swift-specific changes. No affiliation or endorsement is implied.
